= Concrete Models
<refall:concrete-models>
In this section, we sketch some concrete models. All the given models
have types with unrestricted linearity, and so we will write our typing
rules using #emph[un-annotated] contexts and variables $Gamma \, x : A$,
assuming every quantity annotation is $omega$.

== UB
<refall:ssec:ub>
The simplest model exercising all the features of our refinement
calculus is the language with nondeterminism, undefined behavior and
nontermination. We represent this using the monad
$sans(U B) #h(0em) A = cal(P)^(+) \( A union { oo } \) union { arrow.zigzag }$
over sets, with $oo$ a sentinel value for nontermination and
$arrow.zigzag$ for UB. Its ordering is the inclusion order on nonempty
sets $cal(P)^(+) \( A union { oo } \)$ extended with a top element
$arrow.zigzag$. (The full description of this model is in
Appendix~#todo[Cross-reference: `refall:apx:ub`.]) The monadic bind is:
$ arrow.zigzag upright(">>=")_(sans("UB")) f &= arrow.zigzag #h(2em)
  X upright(">>=")_(sans("UB")) f = {f a | a in X} quad upright("if ") forall a in X, f a != arrow.zigzag #h(2em)
  X upright(">>=")_(sans("UB")) f &= arrow.zigzag quad upright("otherwise") $
where we define $f #h(0em) oo = oo$. The Kleisli
category of $sans(U B)$ has the lattice of effects generated by the
nontermination effect $oo$, the UB effect $arrow.zigzag$, and the
nondeterminism effect $?$. In Figure~@refall:fig:ub-submonads, we give the
submonad for each effect, along with its linearity and commutativity
with other effects.

This model lets us interpret instructions
$arrow.zigzag_A : upright(bold(1)) arrow.r_arrow.zigzag A$ analogous to
LLVM's `unreachable` intrinsic. We write $arrow.zigzag$ as shorthand for
$arrow.zigzag_A #h(0em) \( \)$. This instruction lets us define
#emph[unsafe unwrap] operators $rho_l : A + B arrow.r_arrow.zigzag A$
and $rho_r : A + B arrow.r_arrow.zigzag B$ which take the other branch
to $arrow.zigzag$. These satisfy the usual rewrite rules for UB, some of
which are given in Figure~@refall:fig:ub-rewrites.

