== Heaps
<refall:ssec:heaps>
We model a single-threaded heap as a finitely-supported function of type
$S := bb(N) harpoon.rt_(sans(f i n)) bb(N)$. Using the state transformer
on $sans(U B)$, we can define a heap monad
$sans(H e a p) #h(0em) A = S arrow.r sans(U B) #h(0em) \( A times S \)$,
with the natural pointwise partial order. (The full description of this
model is in Appendix~#todo[Cross-reference: `refall:apx:ub-st`.]) Our effect system is the bounded
lattice generated by
${ oo \, arrow.zigzag \, ? \, sans(r) \, sans(w) \, sans(a) }$, with
$sans(r) \, sans(w)$, and $sans(a)$ corresponding to "read", "write",
and "allocate" respectively. The new primitive operations are:

- $sans(l d) : sans(H e a p)_(sans(r) arrow.zigzag) \( bb(N) \, bb(N) \) := lambda p #h(0em) s . sans(i f) #h(0em) p in s #h(0em) sans(t h e n) #h(0em) sans(p u r e)_(sans(N D)) \( s #h(0em) p \, s \) #h(0em) sans(e l s e) #h(0em) arrow.zigzag$

- $sans(s t) : sans(H e a p)_(sans(w) arrow.zigzag) \( bb(N) ⊗ bb(N) \, upright(bold(1)) \) := lambda \( p \, x \) #h(0em) s . sans(i f) #h(0em) p in s #h(0em) sans(t h e n) #h(0em) sans(p u r e)_(sans(N D)) \( \( \) \, \[ p mapsto x \] s \) #h(0em) sans(e l s e) #h(0em) arrow.zigzag$

- $sans(m k) : sans(H e a p)_(sans(a) ?) \( bb(N) \, bb(N) \) := lambda x #h(0em) s . { \( p \, \[ p mapsto x \] s \) divides p in.not s }$

- $sans(r m) : sans(H e a p)_(sans(w) arrow.zigzag) \( bb(N) \, \( \) \) := lambda p . sans(i f) #h(0em) p in s #h(0em) sans(t h e n) #h(0em) s \\ p #h(0em) sans(e l s e) #h(0em) arrow.zigzag$

This model validates the usual properties of heaps (see
Figure~@refall:fig:heap-eqns), as well as that allocation is central, reads and
writes are relevant, and reads are eliminable and commutative.

